<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7469" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cēphēnes</span></b> , um,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κηφῆνες</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>The drones in a swarm of bees</i> (pure Lat. fuci),
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				11, 16, 16, § 48</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphē-nes</span></b> ,
				um, <i>a people of Ethiopia</i> (so
			called from their king, Cepheus), <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5,
			1</span></i> and 97.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphēnus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Ethiopian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proceres,</span>”
				<i>the Ethiopian chiefs</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 764</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
